      "message": "We don\u0027t require openssl 3.5 \n\n\"OpenSSL 3.5 also introduces support for three hybrid ECDH PQ key exchange TLS groups: X25519MLKEM768, SecP256r1MLKEM768 and SecP384r1MLKEM1024.\" \n\nhttps://docs.openssl.org/3.5/man3/SSL_CONF_cmd\n\nWhich is needed for X25519MLKEM768\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/blob/8bd54f0c2f16ba6f5137a047013e5a785b06ccbc/meson.build#L263\n\nAt this point I think it is fine to bump our required openssl version so please do that \n\nThe other choice is something like \n\n```\n#if OPENSSL_VERSION_PREREQ(3, 5)\n    constexpr std::string_view curves \u003d\n        \"X25519MLKEM768:X25519:prime256v1:secp384r1\";\n#else\n    constexpr std::string_view curves \u003d\n        \"X25519:prime256v1:secp384r1\";\n#endif\n```",
      "revId": "bf2702a77b6f10f7bd1ed9f9a559abcfe14d5e3b",
